module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.command_not_found_exit_cannot_distinguish_eviction_from_misnaming

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data command_not_found_exit_cannot_distinguish_eviction_from_misnaming: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "command_not_found_exit_cannot_distinguish_eviction_from_misnaming" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "**POSIX 127 (CommandNotFound) is classified Infra because the exit code cannot distinguish shared-FS eviction of a modelled binary, a misspelled emitted command, or a well-formed command mangled in transit by the wrapper** (INVALID STATE: a subject defect and an environmental miss both present as the same reserved shell status, so gunbc.ci_failure_class classify_failure_exit renders stands-environment for a typo or a wrap mangle as readily as for eviction.",
    "SPECIMEN, review 63442: this PR's wrap ran POSIX quoting and then bash_token_lit quoted again, so sh -c received `'cargo build'` as the command name, would have exited 127, and classify_failure_exit would have called it infra. The modelled command identity at wrap start was present and well-formed; the wrapper mangled it in transit. Caught by review, not by the classifier.",
    "SPECIMEN, gunbc Actions run 34562801087 required-witnesses-floor on srv1-03: D0-ADJUDICATE exited 127 (`target/release/claim_executor: No such file or directory`) after the same job built that binary (Build the witness fold, 06:03) and ran it (D0-MEASURE, 06:06). No planned=/verdict= line and no INTERRUPTED-BEFORE-VERDICT. NAMED CAUSE: runner re-registration on a slot with a job in flight — two runner processes, one `_work` workspace. A concurrent job's Isolate toolchain homes wiped and reinstalled inside the same `_work/_temp` (census: cargo shim mtime 06:37:33 inside a job that installed at 06:03; 34 slots across srv1-4 showed two to four overlapping registrations 06:22–06:48). This is the eviction state of this class, not a fourth POSIX meaning. Main's D0-ADJUDICATE red the same night was FloorRefused native_decl_selection at cpu_deadline 503-508ms against 500ms. The step name merged the two causes. D0-ADJUDICATE was not wrapped, so 127 never became floor_class=infra.",
    "HARM: the instrument built to stop environmental and code failures rendering identically contained a code failure that would have rendered as environmental. A 127 on the wrapped required-lane commands would have silenced the merge floor as stands-environment. Unwrapped D0-ADJUDICATE 127 is the dual: an environmental miss that still reads as the same step name as a FloorRefused.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable — the wrap defect was writable, the classifier had no join, and review was the wall. Host application of runner_unit teardown is outside this row.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed once a 127 can be joined to independent observations that discriminate the three states; the exit code alone cannot, so the class cannot reach structural impossibility from POSIX 127. Per-job runner microVMs make this eviction unwritable by removing the shared `_work` — isolation consequence and the 34562801087 specimen as that plan carries it live on gunbc #10971 07dbb15082 (wise-deer-602); this row does not fork probe dissolution. That is a different path's ceiling, not this classifier's.",
    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, A CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT: join a 127 to (1) an independent observation that the modelled command identity was present at wrap start AND NOT REPLACED DURING the job (toolchain_filesystem_probe start/end pair, or equivalent occupancy of the runner slot), or that the emitted argv inhabits a closed command roster, AND (2) that the serialized wrap argument equals the modelled command bytes. Present-at-wrap-start alone would not have caught review 63442 (quoting) and would not have caught 34562801087 (identity was present at 06:03 and 06:06, destroyed mid-job by another process). That is still the eviction state, not a fourth exit-code meaning. Until those joins exist, 127 stays Infra as an honest-wide arm. 126 is not this class.)",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.ci_failure_class", decl_name: "classify_failure_exit", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.ci_failure_class", decl_name: "wrap_command_with_floor_attempt_receipt_stmts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.bash_build", decl_name: "bash_build_word_lit", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.bash", decl_name: "bash_posix_single_quote_transform", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.witness_floor_workflow", decl_name: "required_ci_measurement_adjudicate_step", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
